{
  "area": "layout-backdrop",
  "description": "The backdrop round a village's terrain (core src/editor/layout/backdrop.ts; the Unreal plugin's BYOA B7 r2 - r5 backdrop, characterised from the math of its spawn code, now Portable/InsimulVillageLayout). Rings of meshes stood evenly round the terrain's rectangle beyond its edge, near sides the ring's distance out, facing the middle with a +-20 degree turn and a scale jitter hashed from each one's place; frame pieces laid as four strips from the terrain's edge out to the piece's own scaled size. Brightwater Vale's 512 m terrain and the B8 project look's ring (16 meshes, 30 m out, jitter 0.3, sunk 2 m); the ring's mesh half-sizes as the editor measured them (the frame's piece is still nominal). Plan frame: IR (x, z) metres, y up; a heading points along (cos h, sin h).",
  "version": 1,
  "sources": [
    {
      "characterisedBy": "insimul-unreal tools/verify-unreal insimul_layout_characterise (Source/InsimulEditor/Tests/layout_characterise.cpp), the Portable code of unreal origin/main 6caede7 (BYOA B0-B8)",
      "ir": "$LOOPS_HOME/unreal/state/world/brightwater-ir-20261017.json",
      "irSha256": "b51cc94a9841462c10905548145cb1bce19d0dc14f75d1facdd2e367e591880d",
      "pairing": "BYOA B8 round 5 (unreal/byoa/state/byoa-b8/round-5): houses by role, the 6 m neighbour gap, the seat sinks, the 2.01 m cast, MI_Landscape_01a's layers and its ground paint",
      "world": "Brightwater Vale (6abb84ae358820954abf1ea2)"
    },
    {
      "cases": "'ring: the B8 look's mountains round Brightwater' (PL.layout-standins, operator ruling U80(3))",
      "measuredBy": "the Unreal editor at unreal 86857a0 (P0.unreal.u23-boxes round 1, WV0 run 2, 2026-11-05): the 36 GB Mac's tools/probe_u23.py over the paired level PairedBrightwater, each ring mesh's half-size max(ext.x, ext.y) / 100 of its GetBoundingBox, to the centimetre: 307.41 (Hills/SM_Mountain_02, 307.4101), 99.96 (Mountain/SM_Mountain_C, 99.9582), 45.13 (Mountain/SM_Mountain_A, 45.1334) and 193.21 (Mountains/SM_Mountain_02, 193.2107) for the look's meshes 0 to 3, where the nominal half-sizes were 180, 240, 150 and 210. The order is the one that stands core's ring where the editor stood it: each of the 16 editor ring meshes, matched to core's placement by its hashed scale, is within 3.5 mm of it in plan and on its heading",
      "record": "$LOOPS_HOME/unreal/state/wv0-1104/p0-unreal-u23-boxes/round-1-builder.md (\"Results\"), standins.txt and runs/main-86857a0-r2/probe.json",
      "writtenBy": "core scripts/restand-layout-corpus.ts --write (scripts/layout-standins.ts): the measured values set, then every expected answer, and every input that is another case's answer (the characteriser's chain), re-derived by core's projection; a value is rewritten only where it moved past the file's tolerance"
    }
  ],
  "tolerance": 0.000001,
  "angleKeys": ["heading"],
